{
  "_comment": "Single source of truth linking Doc 1's logic to the building (Doc 4 §15). The game is one continuous walk: each scene's branch names the ROOM it is played in (data/rooms.json) and its two THRESHOLDS -- zones in that room the candidate walks to; stepping into one commits the choice (src/director.js). A threshold's `exit` is the door that opens onto `via` (a CN_* connector) with the next scene's room joined behind it; when the next scene's room is the same set (S1 -> S2, S5 C -> S6 C, S6 H -> S7 H) the scene changes where he stands. `next` is per branch and the same for both thresholds: the spine never forks, only the render does (state.js renderFor). Beats (`beat`, `onEnter`, `approach`) are run in order: sfxCue, oneShot, caption, rattle, open/close (door), show/hide (prop), light, screen, setFlag, hold/drop (a prop in his hands), actor, lookAt, sit, moveTo, shot, ride, shake, seal, waitMs. The mini-games are gone (the author's call); friction now comes from how he walks to the choice (src/friction.js).",
  "spineOrder": [
    "S0",
    "S1",
    "S2",
    "S3",
    "S4",
    "S5",
    "S6",
    "S7",
    "S8"
  ],
  "_musicNote": "`music` (scene-level, or a per-branch override): 'muzak' | 'pad' | 'deep' | 'water' | {file} | null. Generated live by src/music.js on audio.js's music bus -- no licensed tracks. See the music.js header.",
